      "writtenOn": "2022-02-25T17:35:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "See below, I think you should combine the input/output compatible nodes.\n\nThen you can set `#define DT_DRV_COMPAT x96_ap_pwrseq_gpio` and then use `DT_INST_FOREACH_STATUS_OKAY` as the iterator.\n\nI think you can use `DT_INST_NODE_HAS_PROP` to check for an input boolean property.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 11,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 13,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "bd7c7ba41d3e9171aafeccf28e9b8a47b832ee54",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "60c0357b_cff04fcd",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/ap_pwrseq/signal_gpio.c",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 13,
      "author": {
        "id": 1281040
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-26T00:09:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yep, I agree that keeping it separate is likely not a huge benefit.\nIt just saved a bit of space, and was possibly premature optimisation.\n\nSo the use of DT_DRV_COMPAT is a little tricky.\nThe current code uses this to access the main node (intel_ap_pwrseq) which has the config like timing values etc.\nSo there will be some collisions in files like signal_vw.c\n\nUsing DT_DRV_COMPAT also makes the node access a bit awkward - the macros get passed an instance number rather than the node, and then you need to use DT_INST_PROP along with the instance. This isn\u0027t a big deal, but the colliding DT_DRV_COMPAT is a bit hard to work around.\n\nDT_DRV_COMPAT seems to be great for defining real devices and drivers, but for more generic device tree config, it\u0027s not a great fit (especially when dealing concurrently with multiple compatibles).\nI tried to clean it up by creating separate guards for each signal source, and doing a funky MY_COMPAT for signal_gpio.c and signal_vw.c\nNone of this gets exposed outside these files.",
      "parentUuid": "2c17f9c1_7bd2138e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 11,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 13,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "bd7c7ba41d3e9171aafeccf28e9b8a47b832ee54",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
